g=[[4]*9 for _ in range(19)]
vals={2:[0,1,4,5],3:[0],4:[2,3,4,5],5:[5],6:[0,5],7:[0,5],8:[0,3,5]}
for r,cs in vals.items():
 for c in cs:g[r][c]=3
# add 2 between consecutive marker cells in each row/column
for r in range(19):
 cs=[c for c,x in enumerate(g[r]) if x==3]
 for a,b in zip(cs,cs[1:]):
  for c in range(a+1,b):
   if g[r][c]==4:g[r][c]=2
for c in range(9):
 rs=[r for r in range(19) if g[r][c]==3]
 for a,b in zip(rs,rs[1:]):
  for r in range(a+1,b):
   if g[r][c]==4:g[r][c]=2
print('\n'.join(' '.join(map(str,row)) for row in g))
